# open-cave port: COMPLETE — 107/107, then the curmudgeon rename

## What this is

`c:\github\shoddy\mills\open-cave\` is a from-scratch port of ESR's open-adventure
(BSD-2-Clause C, at `c:\github\open-adventure-master`) into Shoddy. The goal was
**107/107 byte-exact** against the C's recorded test transcripts in
`c:\github\open-adventure-master\tests\*.chk`.

**Achieved: 107/107, mean prefix 1255 (full length). Both suites green:**
`dotnet test src/Shoddy.Tests/Shoddy.Tests.csproj` 112/112, and
`mill run test.shoddy` passes. `SHODDY_LINT=1` shows 66 warnings, all
pre-existing and benign (string constants that case-fold onto accessors).

## The curmudgeon rename (2026-07-26)

The cave's little knife-throwing cave folk are curmudgeons now. Upstream's
name for them is gone from the mill everywhere — data, generated tables,
code, comments and prose — and this file keeps it that way, so it is spelled
nowhere below. Find it with a case-insensitive grep of
`c:\github\open-adventure-master\` when you need it.

Consequence: **`*.chk` is no longer the pass/fail oracle.** 107/107 was
re-verified by diffing this build against a pre-rename build of the same
sources, not against upstream. Any future re-measure must do the same, or
substitute the new name into the `.chk` files first.

Five upstream logs *type* the old name (grep the `tests/` directory for
it), so they now draw `Sorry, I don't know the word ...`; substituting the
new name into the log restores the old transcript exactly. `saveresume.4`
needs its own working directory — save files collide if the suite is run in
parallel from one cwd.

Two details the rename turned up and that are easy to get wrong again:

- Vocabulary is stored **already cut to five letters**, so the object's old
  two-word synonym list collapses to the single stem `{ "curmu" }`. A
  longer spelling in a `words:` list would silently match nothing;
  test.shoddy now asserts both singular and plural classify as an object.
- The prose in `adventure.yaml` is hand-wrapped at ~70 columns and is
  printed verbatim, so lengthening a word means re-wrapping its paragraph.
  Nine message blocks and two room descriptions were reflowed, which is
  why `cave-locations.shoddy` grew two lines.

## How to re-measure

Harness (persists from earlier sessions):

    C:\Users\foster\AppData\Local\Temp\claude\c--github-shoddy\708844e1-7031-471d-be5c-03126ba68699\scratchpad\

    powershell -NoProfile -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File "<scratchpad>\measure.ps1" -Out rNN.txt -Throttle 8

Latest result file: r61.txt (`== PASS 107 / 107  mean-prefix 1255`).
Always compare mean prefix as well as pass count; diagnose only at the
first divergence; run the real `advent` under WSL rather than reasoning
about C behaviour (misc.c:769 is patched to trace random draws — restore
from misc.c.bak before any upstream diffing).

## What the final session fixed (46 → 107)

In rough order: Destroy now sweeps every room list (two-ended objects);
troll payment juggles CHASM and leaves prop UNPAID; chain()/unlock-chain;
game.panic + exit-closed gating in do_move and grate; drop specials
(gem-in-cavity + rug hover with a movable second placement, coins→batteries,
bear-routs-troll, cage-drops-bird, bird-vs-dragon); FEE FIE FOE FOO egg
message indices; urn fill/light/extinguish/pour; FLY and the hovering rug
(which is immovable while hovering); gem take re-opens the cavity;
lampcheck runs during closing (skipped only on the two transition turns,
and the cave-closed turn swallows the typed command); repository stocking
stashifies props (negative) with the per-prompt unstash pass and oyster
clue line; ObjectWord alias chain in C order (curmudgeon, liquids-unless-closed,
oil→urn, plant2, knife, rod→rod2); death by travel to location 0; BLAST +
bonus + full closing/closed/Witt's-End/clue scoring; bird weightlessness;
GO intransitive "Where?"; per-prompt knife expiry and no phantom-knife
revival; attack target ambiguity counting (enemies outrank bird/vend/clam,
throw excludes bird/vend); silent_yes_or_no retry loop; throw-axe at
dragon/troll/ogre/bear; "west"×10 counts second words too; enter-water;
>2-word and empty-line input handling at the prompt (no turn cost);
z'zzz placeholder is not a vocab word; BREAK (mirror/vase) and WAKE curmudgeon
→ GO_CURMUDGEONWAKE endings; SCORE verb; WASTE verb; INVENTORY-with-object is
FIND, listing skips the bear but appends the tame-bear line; read-oyster
endgame clue (Clshnt, −10); croak during closng is final; floor→ground
rewrite when outdoors (listing only — C does it in speak(); extend
Grounded() to other sites if a new divergence ever shows it); SlayDragon
sweeps everything in the canyon to LOC_SECRET5; stashed caged bird taking;
ordinary travel now maintains OldLc2 so "back" can retrace through Foof
rooms; plover transport (special 2) drops the emerald and re-travels;
MESSAG take; repository sign prop is 1 (ENDGAME_SIGN); RunVerb records
the object into PendObj so Cleared can move it to OldObj (the bird hint
reads it there).

New Game fields this session: Panic, Bonus, Clshnt (Panic is persisted in
the save format; Bonus/Clshnt are not — blast and the clue can't survive
into a save that matters). Fate gained `Won` (endgame mode: +4 like Died).

## Language traps that cost time (all still true)

- `Else` requires an indented block; no `else if` — use helper Defs.
- `mill run test.shoddy` does NOT parse cave.shoddy. After every edit:
  `cd <sandbox>/tests && echo n | mill run <abs path>/cave.shoddy | head -2`
- Field accessors lose every name contest (run SHODDY_LINT=1 after adding
  Defs/Types; 66 pre-existing warnings is the baseline).
- Record constructors are positional — NewGame is the single positional
  Game() site; adding a field means one insertion there too.
- **Always verify a tag exists before dispatching on it** — this session
  `MotionNamed("PLOVE")` silently missed (tag is "PLOVER") and cost a run.
- A recursive void Def's base case must emit nothing.

